<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ince Minareli Madrasa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1264</span> · Also known as İnce Minareli Medrese, Ince Minareli Medrese</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ince Minareli <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madrasa">Madrasa</a>, the madrasa of the slender minaret, is a Seljuk theological college in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konya">Konya</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>, built around 1264 for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">vizier</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahib-ata-fakhr-al-din-ali">Sahib Ata Fakhr al-Din Ali</a>. It is famous for its elaborately carved stone portal with bands of inscription. Its tall minaret was largely destroyed by lightning in 1901, and the building now houses a museum of stone and wood carving.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ince-minareli-madrasa.jpg" alt="Ince Minareli Madrasa" width="320" height="220" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bernard Gagnon · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ince_Minareli_Medrese_01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
